 "note": "The level 1 map (schema 3): a 96 x 48 cell village drawn at three quarters zoom (18 px cells, view.zoom 0.75; the player sees up to 72 x 27 cells around the barracks). defense_02's compound, wall ring, openings, entries and socket order moved onto a bigger map with the three defense points further out (left x=29, top y=15, right x=65) so a section has room for its defenders and sockets, and the entries (left x=6, top y=0, right x=88) three or more cells outside the window. The infantry barracks (the one required objective) stands in the centre, ten civilian houses (v01..v08 at their OpenRA footprints) form a ring around it, and ten civilians (eight technicians, a man and a woman) wander inside the wander rectangle. Rows 25 and 26 stay clear from the left opening to the right one and columns 44..49 stay clear above the barracks, so every opening has a lane of at least two cells to the barracks exit (checked by the generator with a flood fill). No command core, factory, power plant or radar dome.",
